WEBVTT

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.260
I see...

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.390
So it failed.

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.060
Regrettably.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:30.440
He's a real thorn in my side. And he cannot be dealt with through normal means.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:31.070
Yes sir.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:34.860
But everyone has a weakness.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:39.280
A weak point buried deep within their instincts.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.990
That's right.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.160
Where's our next soldier?

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.120
We're preparing him as we speak.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.000
Good. We also need more soldiers.

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:49.290
Yes sir.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.380
Don't let me down.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.930
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:03.060
wondering what I should do right now.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.520
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:14.070
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:19.700
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:25.120
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:29.580
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:35.880
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.180
Oh someday - one of these days

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:45.260
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:51.350
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.940
depend on me for your repairs.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:01.320
So faraway - let's run!

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:07.540
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:11.830
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:17.880
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:27.770
Fearless

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.740
Please fasten your seat belts!

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:49.750
Everyone, the main controls of the aircraft has suffered a partial system failure.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:57.250
We are now attempting an emergency landing. We are specially trained to handle these situations.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:58.840
Please remain calm.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:02.430
I'm dreaming.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.870
Let us out now!

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.340
The brakes aren't working?!

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.130
What now?

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.850
It's over! I'm done for!

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.590
<i>Plastic explosives in the back molars?</i>

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:20.370
What the heck-?!

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:43.980
A survivor of an airplane crash that caused 23 casualties has suddenly gone missing.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:48.690
The authorities are treating this case as a possible abduction.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:57.740
So Mr. Aaron Maxwell, the survivor of that airliner crash, has gone missing, huh?

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.960
Don't scare me like that for God's sake!

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.960
Any luck with the probe?

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:08.840
Yeah, it's just like you suspected.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:11.970
The janitor in that elevator survived a shipwreck.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:16.300
That retiree on the train was rescued from a helicopter tour that made a hard landing.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:20.930
Not only that, the both of them have later gone missing.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:25.980
Then they pop out of nowhere trying to ice you. Hardly a coincidence, right?

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:29.230
Take a look at this woman.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:36.490
"Car Driving On Mt. Rainier Plummets. Driver Anne Brown Suffers Minor Injuries."

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:43.710
I see... so this woman also miraculously survived a freak accident.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.460
Guess it's Seattle for me.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:48.630
Also, one more thing.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:53.760
Through the internet? That's gonna cost extra.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:09:00.640
...Actually, you already paid me a fair amount for this probe.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.730
I'll be waiting for your call.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:18.660
This must be it.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.960
Miss Brown?! Miss Anne Brown?!

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:30.250
And I came at this hour expecting her to be home.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:35.010
Hey, let go!

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:36.840
What are you doing?

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.050
Anne?

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:55.070
They swept her away right in front of me!

00:09:55.530 --> 00:10:00.950
They're likely the same bunch that abducted the others. But the question is why?

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.080
Hold on a minute.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.380
I just got some info!

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.050
Where's the location?

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:20.930
Hey, let me handle it! I'm getting that info out of him!

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:33.230
I'll ask once more: where's the location?

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:36.610
I can't win with you, Christ.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:48.620
So you're "Blue Fire."

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:55.050
You're the first person I've met who's not surprised that I'm still a kid.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:59.550
Your info is solid, right? Then
your age or sex doesn't matter.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:01.640
Gotta admire your thinking.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:06.390
We can't talk here, so come with me.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:24.280
I hack into the FBI computers as a hobby.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:30.000
That's how I got my hands on their investigative reports relating to the abductions.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.880
Solbeno, huh?

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:37.170
You know about him? Then that speeds up the conversation.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:39.010
Igeri Solbeno.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:44.890
Former KGB agent. We don't see a lot of him due to his photophobia.

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:49.810
He has an abnormal hatred toward a certain sniper that ruined a mission.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:55.650
He immigrated here following the Soviet collapse along with his former KGB subordinates.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:12:00.150
The FBI believes that he's going after this sniper.

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:03.030
Pull up the data they have on Solbeno's people.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:15.000
Those abductees were literally The Chosen Ones.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:21.670
They've lost any sense of fear after being
scared witless during those freak accidents.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.430
Fearless.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:29.520
That's right. And Solbeno discovered the value of that fearlessness.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:33.440
He's using them as soldiers that don't fear death!

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:36.110
No, that's not right.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:40.440
It's not that those soldiers don't fear death, they just don't think of it.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:41.440
Even at that...

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:46.700
...the sniper Solbeno is going after is still alive, isn't he?

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:51.450
And a woman they think has that
fearlessness was recently abducted.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:56.130
And that sniper is still alive? Awesome!

00:12:56.130 --> 00:13:01.460
I'd like to meet that sniper just once! Don't you think so too, mister?

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.140
Don't care which way, huh?

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:11.680
Well, it doesn't really matter to me how you use that info.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:16.400
Thanks for that service fee. Now I can finally upgrade my computer.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:19.480
The allowance my mom gives me would've never covered it.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:30.990
Christ, what a kid. So what are you planning on doing?

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:37.120
Spread the word that I'm going to the city where Solbeno's hiding.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:41.000
Wha- you're gonna face those guy? Alone?

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:14.870
Don't turn on the lights!

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.660
Please forgive me.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.040
I thought you weren't here.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:28.380
Why are you doing this to me?

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:32.430
Because you survived a serious accident.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:35.560
Are you scared?

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.230
Huh?

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.150
She's fearless.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:50.660
Just as I thought, Anne. You're fearless.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:52.120
Fearless?

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:56.500
Right now, you have absolutely no sense of fear.

00:14:56.500 --> 00:15:03.170
The terror you went through during that serious accident broke down the primal phobic programming in your brain.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:05.170
I have no fear?

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:12.140
People who possess instinctual fear would
normally shut their eyes reflexively and scream.

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:15.310
But you don't feel a thing.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:22.020
You will receive special training in order to become my soldier.

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:23.190
Soldier?

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:28.650
You will kill the sniper called Golgo 13
who has caused me great pains.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:31.200
You'll become my first-class soldier.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:34.200
That has nothing to do with me!

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:37.580
Yes, absolutely nothing.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:42.210
But the drugs I gave you will have you following my every order.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.050
Train her well.

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:47.670
Yes sir.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:50.050
What about the man?

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:52.680
He's going through the training as you instructed.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:57.720
Soon, my soldiers will kill that man.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:18.240
He's here.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.870
He's heading for the hotel just as we anticipated.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:31.510
I shall take your luggage.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:39.060
This way.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.060
Thank you very much.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:56.990
Who's there?

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:57.740
The bellboy!

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:02.410
My apologies, I forgot to tell you about the amenities provided by your room.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.000
You can speak from there.

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:07.960
I hear what you're saying, but I
need to be in view of the facilities.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:40.990
Hey, what's going on?

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:04.520
Good evening.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:08.730
Has the vehicle I rented from NB Rental Cars arrived yet?

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:10.730
Yeah, I was holding it for you.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:45.640
Did something happen?

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:15.920
Th-They've failed. Our soldiers
went after him at the same time...

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.670
...but Golgo's still alive.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:38.320
<i>He didn't notice me.</i>

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:42.700
<i>Since he has just avoided all
those attacks, I can kill him now.</i>

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:52.120
Now!

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:32.960
<i>He took out my perfect soldiers.</i>

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:36.960
<i>Does this mean... he has absolutely no weakness?</i>

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:40.130
<i>He's coming.</i>

00:20:51.730 --> 00:20:57.020
Splendid work, Golgo 13. Do you remember me?

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:02.360
I'm not going to put up a fight now that you're here.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:05.410
It's over. I've accepted my fate.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:09.830
As you know, I cannot stand bright lights.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:14.580
Forgive me for having us meet in this dark room.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:20.000
I'll turn on the lights now and you can shoot me.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:24.300
But please don't expose me to the light for too long.

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:27.930
It's my last wish as a man who's about to die.

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:43.110
H-How did you know I was right here?

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:49.370
A voice from a speaker is not the same as the real thing.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:53.120
No matter how precise the equipment.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:55.040
But why?

00:21:56.040 --> 00:22:03.760
Why weren't you killed by my perfect soldiers who didn't fear death?

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:09.510
Fear of death... and fear itself are the only things that keep us from danger.

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:16.520
One is able to survive as long as he fears death.

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:19.860
That's why I'm here standing.

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:45.710
I enjoyed the little things.

00:22:47.760 --> 00:22:52.930
I loved when you gave me a flower every day

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:59.020
instead of just one big bouquet

00:22:59.730 --> 00:23:03.860
of flowers.

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:11.490
It was like a romance novel.

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:16.080
Surely someday... just kidding.

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:19.460
I had a dream.

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:25.170
Your face shined eternally.

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:31.760
Because I think of you all the time.

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:37.310
I'm sorry, but on a lonely night like this

00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:43.810
I'm remembering you, but

00:23:44.110 --> 00:23:48.400
I won't cry like I did that day.

00:23:50.150 --> 00:23:51.570
I won't.

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:06.380
One rainy day, Golgo met Cecilia, a woman with a dark past.

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:10.340
The two met again by chance on the same flight.

00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:13.970
But they became caught up in an incident on that plane.

00:24:13.970 --> 00:24:19.810
Cecilia was aggressively captivated by
Golgo in that dangerous situation, but...

00:24:19.810 --> 00:24:24.350
Next time on Golgo 13: Love Moans on an Arctic Night.

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:26.150
Love Moans on an Arctic Night

00:24:24.350 --> 00:24:28.690
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
